  "notes": "West leads the ♥A against 4♠. West cashes 2 heart tricks and continues a third round, South ruffing. South's problem is to avoid the loss of 2 trump tricks.\n\nThe normal play with this suit combination is to cash the ♠A and lead low from dummy towards South's holding. On this deal, however, this play is not correct. There are only 17 outstanding high card points. West must have the ♠K for his 1NT opening bid (which shows 15-17 high card points).\n\nSouth should start by leading the ♠Q from his hand. As long as West began with fewer than 4 spades, South will be able to hold his trump losers to one.\n\nOn the above lie of the cards, South can also succeed by passing a low spade through West. This play is not correct as there is room for East to have a singleton ♠J and West to still have a 1NT opening bid. If East is allowed to win a singleton ♠J, West will still have a certain trump trick.",
